cks by overlaying their waveforms.`,inputs:{audio1:{name:`audio1`},audio2:{name:`audio2`},merge_method:{name:`merge_method`,tooltip:`The method used to combine the audio waveforms.`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},lgn={display_name:`Bake Ambient Occlusion`,description:`Bakes an ambient-occlusion map from a high-poly mesh into a low-poly's UV layout (white = open, dark = crevices). Feed the UV-unwrapped low_poly and the high_poly it was decimated from. Outputs a grayscale image for Apply Texture To Mesh's occlusion input (packed into the ORM map / occlusionTexture).`,inputs:{low_poly:{name:`low_poly`},high_poly:{name:`high_poly`},resolution:{name:`resolution`},samples:{name:`samples`,tooltip:`Rays per texel. More = smoother, slower. Raise if grainy.`},max_distance:{name:`max_distance`,tooltip:`Ray length, as a fraction of the bounding box diagonal. Smaller = tighter, more local occlusion.`},strength:{name:`strength`,tooltip:`Scales the occlusion. >1 darkens, <1 lightens.`},bias:{name:`bias`,tooltip:`Ray origin lift off the surface, as a fraction of the bounding box diagonal. Raise if even surfaces show dark blotches/holes.`}},outputs:{0:{name:`occlusion`,tooltip:null}}},ugn={display_name:`Bake Normal Map from Mesh`,description:`Bakes a tangent-space normal map (glTF/OpenGL +Y) from a high-poly mesh into a low-poly's UV layout, capturing detail lost during decimation. Feed the UV-unwrapped low_poly and the high_poly it was decimated from. Outputs an image for Apply Texture To Mesh's normal_map input.`,inputs:{low_poly:{name:`low_poly`},high_poly:{name:`high_poly`},resolution:{name:`resolution`},cage_distance:{name:`cage_distance`,tooltip:`Surface search band, as a fraction of the bounding box diagonal. Raise for wrong/missing patches under heavy decimation; lower if it grabs across gaps.`},ignore_backfaces:{name:`ignore_backfaces`,tooltip:`Skip high-poly surfaces facing away from the texel, so crevices/enclosed spaces don't grab the opposite wall. Disable only if the high-poly winding is inconsistent.`}},outputs:{0:{name:`normal_map`,tooltip:null}}},dgn={display_name:`Bake Texture From Voxel`,description:`Bakes PBR textures onto the mesh's existing UV layout (trilinear-sample the sparse voxel volume). Does NOT unwrap — connect a UV unwrap node upstream. Outputs base_color + metallic/roughness grayscale IMAGEs (black if no PBR); feed them to ApplyTextureToMesh (SAME mesh) for SaveGLB.`,inputs:{mesh:{name:`mesh`},voxel_colors:{name:`voxel_colors`},texture_size:{name:`texture_size`,tooltip:`Square UV atlas resolution.`},reference_mesh:{name:`reference_mesh`,tooltip:`Optional dense pre-decimation mesh; back-projects each texel onto its true surface before sampling, removing faceted baking on coarse meshes.`}},outputs:{0:{name:`base_color`,tooltip:null},1:{name:`metallic`,tooltip:null},2:{name:`roughness`,tooltip:null}}},fgn={display_name:`Basic Guider`,inputs:{model:{name:`model`},conditioning:{name:`conditioning`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},pgn={display_name:`BasicScheduler`,inputs:{model:{name:`model`},scheduler:{name:`scheduler`},steps:{name:`steps`},denoise:{name:`denoise`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},mgn={display_name:`Batch Images`,inputs:{images:{name:`images`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},hgn={display_name:`Batch Latents`,inputs:{latents:{name:`latents`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},ggn={display_name:`Batch Masks`,inputs:{masks:{name:`masks`}},outputs:{0:{tooltip:null}}},_gn={display_name:`Beeble SwitchX Image Edit`,description:`Edit a single image with Beeble SwitchX. Switches anything in the scene (background, lighting, costume) while preserving the original subject's pixels. Provide a reference image and/or text prompt to describe the new look. Max ~2.77MP.`,inputs:{image:{name:`image`},prompt:{name:`prompt`,tooltip:`Text description of the desired output (max 2000 chars). At least one of 'prompt' or 'reference_image' is required.`},alpha_mode:{name:`alpha_mode`,tooltip:`Controls how SwitchX decides what to keep vs. regenerate. 'auto' isolates the main subject automatically. 'fill' regenerates the entire frame while preserving geometry. 'select' propagates a first-frame keyframe across the clip. 'custom' uses a per-frame alpha matte you provide.`},max_resolution:{name:`max_resolution`,tooltip:`Maximum output resolution.`},seed:{name:`seed`,tooltip:`Seed controls whether the node should re-run; results are non-deterministic regardless of seed.`},reference_image:{name:`reference_image`,tooltip:`Reference image whose look (background, lighting, costume) the result should adopt. At least one of 'reference_image' or 'prompt' is required.`},control_after_generate:{name:`control after generate`}},outputs:{0:{name:`image`,tooltip:null},1:{name:`alpha`,tooltip:`The alpha matte Beeble used. Empty for 'fill' mode, which has no separate matte.`}}},vgn={display_name:`Beeble SwitchX Video Edit`,description:`Edit a video with Beeble SwitchX. Switches anything in the scene (background, lighting, costume) while preserving the original subject's pixels and motion. Provide a reference image and/or text prompt to describe the new look. Max 240 frames, max ~2.77MP per frame.`,inputs:{video:{name:`video`},prompt:{name:`prompt`,tooltip:`Text description of the desired output (max 2000 chars). At least one of 'prompt' or 'reference_image' is required.`},alpha_mode:{name:`alpha_mode`,tooltip:`Controls how SwitchX decides what to keep vs. regenerate. 'auto' isolates the main subject automatically. 'fill' regenerates the entire frame while preserving geometry. 'select' propagates a first-frame keyframe across the clip. 'custom' uses a per-frame alpha matte you provide.`},max_resolution:{name:`max_resolution`,tooltip:`Maximum output resolution.`},seed:{name:`seed`,tooltip:`Seed controls whether the node should re-run; results are non-deterministic regardless of seed.`},reference_image:{name:`reference_image`,tooltip:`Reference image whose look (background, lighting, costume) the result should adopt. At least 